    "explanation": "This dispute is about the 5.00 SGD no-show cancellation fee on trip TRP-05064. The fee was charged to the rider at 15:49:04 on 2026-09-06 and then reversed at 19:30 — refunded to the rider and withheld from the driver — so the live question is whether the driver was entitled to that 5.00 SGD. The case cannot be decided on this record and goes to a human reviewer.\n\nWhy. The driver's case stands on the free-wait rule, POL-NS-21: a driver may cancel as a rider no-show only after waiting 5 minutes (300 s) from arriving at the pickup. The trip record (EV-TRIP-05064, weight 1.0) shows the arrival marker at 15:42:00 and the cancellation at 15:49:00, 420 seconds later, and the driver is right about that arithmetic. But POL-NS-21 requires both the trip record and the GPS trace, and this category's own arrival test makes the driver 'at the pickup' only when the trip record's arrival event is corroborated by the GPS trace within 50 m of the pickup. That trace (EV-GPS-05064, weight 0.6, issue code GPS_GAP_STRADDLING_CANCELLATION — named here as POL-GEN-02(3) requires) has a single 720-second gap from 15:38:00 to 15:50:00 that covers the arrival marker, the entire waiting window and the cancellation; it reports arrival_check.corroborated = false with no nearest fix. The one artifact that could confirm the driver was there is impaired over exactly the stretch in question, so the arrival — and with it whether the free wait ever began — is undecided on this record, not disproved. I therefore reject the driver's argument that the clean trip record alone establishes arrival: the policy's arrival test reads both artifacts, and the trip record's arrival event is the driver's own button tap, which POL-NS-21 makes out only where the trace corroborates it.\n\nWhat follows for the money. A fact POL-NS-21 needs — when the driver arrived — cannot be established because the evidence that would carry it is impaired. POL-GEN-26 sends that to a human reviewer, and POL-NS-26 expressly subjects the finality of a no-show ruling to POL-GEN-26. So the case is escalated: no money issues either way, the 5.00 SGD currently sits with the rider (fee_reversed at 19:30, payment_status REFUNDED, refund_issued_sgd 5.00) and is held there pending review, and the reviewer decides the arrival question. My confidence is capped at 0.6, the weight of the impaired GPS artifact the escalation rests on. No referral fires: the fee on record is exactly the policy 5.00 SGD (EV-FARE-05064), so POL-NS-22's fee-amount check adds nothing; the rider's profile shows no repeat no-show count under POL-NS-25; and POL-NS-24's goodwill credit is not engaged. The absent traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-05064-01, weight 0.0) carries no fact and is not relied on.\n\nWhat is not in issue. The driver's contact obligation under POL-NS-23 is met — two in-app messages (15:42:20 and 15:46:00, both read) and one in-app call (15:45:10, 25 s, unanswered), all before the 15:49:00 cancellation — so there is no FULL_REFUND on that ground, and both parties accept it. POL-NS-24 does not apply: this was an on-demand trip with no scheduled time, the rider did not cancel, and the driver did attempt contact, so neither a refund nor the 5.00 SGD goodwill credit arises. The driver's account, the rider's account (that he was standing at Blk 33 and never saw the car) and the chat log (EV-CHAT-05064, weight 1.0) were all considered; none of them places the driver at the pickup or settles it, which is why the question goes to a human reviewer rather than being decided here."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "POL-NS-22 charges the 5.00 SGD fee only 'when the driver cancels after the free wait'. Where the start of that wait — the driver's arrival at the pickup — is unproven, that precondition fails and the fee is not engaged. The driver is the filing party here (dispute.filed_by = DRIVER), and on the money record the 5.00 SGD has already gone back to the rider and been withheld from the driver (fee_reversed at 2026-09-06T19:30:00+08:00; payment_status REFUNDED; refund_issued_sgd 5.00). The driver's claim is not supported and the present state stands: NO_ACTION under POL-GEN-03, which is party-relative and never restores a charge, leaving the disputed 5.00 where it already sits — with the rider.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-GPS-05064 at weight_multiplier 0.6 but does not name its issue code(s): GPS_GAP_STRADDLING_CANCELLATION"
    },
    {
      "claim": "If the Tribunal will not simply find the arrival unproven, POL-GEN-26 governs: 'when the driver arrived' is a fact POL-NS-21 needs, and the evidence that would carry it is impaired — the single trace of the driver's movement has a 720 s hole sitting exactly over the arrival marker and over the whole waiting window, leaving no fix within the arrival radius. POL-GEN-26 requires the case to be escalated with the open question stated, and POL-NS-26 expressly subjects the finality of a no-show ruling to POL-GEN-26. ESCALATE is terminal and holds the amount rather than collecting it, so the rider continues not to carry the 5.00 SGD.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-GPS-05064 at weight_multiplier 0.6 but does not name its issue code(s): GPS_GAP_STRADDLING_CANCELLATION"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The only artifact capable of placing the driver at the pickup is EV-GPS-05064, at weight 0.6. Under POL-GEN-02(2) the confidence in any finding that the driver was at the pickup cannot exceed that 0.6, and under POL-GEN-02(3) any ruling leaning on it must name it, its weight and its issue code. A DRIVER_COMPENSATION ruling restoring the fee to the driver would have to rest on a fact this record cannot carry at full weight, and the impairment must not be airbrushed out of the reasoning.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-GPS-05064 at weight_multiplier 0.6 but does not name its issue code(s): GPS_GAP_STRADDLING_CANCELLATION"
