    "explanation": "To both of you: this dispute is about the 5.00 SGD no-show fee charged on trip TRP-05064 and the 5.00 SGD already moved back to the rider and withheld from the driver (fee_reversed at 2026-09-06T19:30:00+08:00, refund_issued_sgd 5.00). I cannot decide it on this record, so I am sending it to a human reviewer with the 5.00 SGD held rather than refunded or collected.\n\nWhat is settled. The driver's contact obligation (POL-NS-23) is met and no one now disputes it: two in-app chat messages (15:42:20 and 15:46:00, both read) on EV-CHAT-05064 and one in-app call placed at 15:45:10 on EV-TRIP-05064, all before the 15:49:00 cancellation; the clause requires a call to be placed, not answered. Both artifacts are complete at weight 1.00, so there is no full refund on this ground. POL-NS-24 does not apply: this was an on-demand trip with no scheduled time (trip_record.scheduled_at is null), the rider did not cancel, and the driver did attempt contact, so neither the driver-no-show refund nor the 5.00 SGD goodwill credit arises. The fee on the record is exactly the 5.00 SGD policy fee (EV-FARE-05064, fee_matches_policy true), so the POL-NS-22 non-standard-amount referral does not fire, and no rider no-show counter is present in the profile, so the POL-NS-25 repeat-no-show referral does not fire.\n\nWhat is not settled. One fact decides whether the 5.00 SGD fee stands: was the driver actually at the pickup, so that the 300-second free wait under POL-NS-21 ever began? This category's arrival test answers that only where the trip record's arrival marker is corroborated by the GPS trace inside the 50 m pickup radius. It is not corroborated. EV-GPS-05064 is impaired (weight 0.60, issue GPS_GAP_STRADDLING_CANCELLATION): a single 720-second gap from 15:38:00 to 15:50:00 that swallows the 15:42:00 arrival marker, the whole waiting window and the 15:49:00 cancellation, with no fix anywhere inside the 50 m radius (nearest_fix null, corroborated false).\n\nOn the parties' arguments. Driver: the 420 seconds from the arrival marker to cancellation, and the clean trip record, do not by themselves make the free wait out - POL-NS-21's arrival limb is tested by the arrival test, and an arrival tap is a status the driver set, which records only that he set it; the twice-repeated chat messages were sent inside the hole, so they stand in for the missing trace rather than replacing it. The driver's further argument that the arrival fact is carried by the 1.00-weight trip record therefore fails, and with it the DRIVER_COMPENSATION claim: I accept that the fee matches the policy fee, but the free-wait precondition it depends on is undecided, not proved. Rider: your point that the trace is impaired rather than merely uncorroborated is accepted, and your POL-GEN-26 point is accepted - the free-wait start is not established.\n\nThat is exactly POL-GEN-26's case: 'when the driver arrived' is a fact POL-NS-21 needs, and the evidence that would carry it is impaired. POL-NS-26 makes the finality of a no-show ruling subject to POL-GEN-26. An undecided fact supports neither a payment that needs the clause to hold nor a refund that needs it to fail, so I move no money. The open question for the human reviewer is whether the driver was at Block 33, Jalan Bukit Merah between 15:42:00 and 15:49:00. Confidence is capped at 0.60 by the impaired GPS trace (POL-GEN-02(2)); the dispute value of 5.00 SGD would otherwise leave the AI ruling final."
  },
